      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X\\sim U[2,10],$ find $\\textrm{Var}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(b-a)^2}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=2$ and $b=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(10-2)^2}{12} = \\dfrac{64}{12} = \\dfrac{16}{3}.\n$$",
